      "id": "2073317355673862569",
      "text": "THIS GUY BUILT A FULL IPHONE APP WITH FABLE 5 BEFORE HIS USAGE CREDITS RAN OUT\n\nan agency would've charged $25,000-$80,000 for this\n\nFable 5 did it in one session\n\nthe idea: a voice note transcription app for creative thinking\n\nAI-analyzed transcripts. chat with your own notes. built from scratch\n\nthe setup:\n\n> Fable 5 = orchestrator only, high effort, no escalation\n> all implementation delegated to Opus sub-agents\n> design first, architecture second - backwards from normal dev, but the design WAS the product\n\nthe workflow:\n\n- mocked up glassmorphism UI in HTML/CSS - nailed it first try\n- ran an A/B test vs Opus 4.8 - Opus was surprisingly good too\n- extracted design tokens from the mockup into a shared theme\n- ported everything to React Native pixel-for-pixel\n- deployed straight to his phone via Expo + Apple Developer account\n\nthe difference:\n\nOpus needed rounds and rounds of revisions\n\nFable just... got it, every piece of feedback, executed correctly the first time\n\nfrom idea to working iPhone app, one session\n\nhave you tried building anything with Fable 5 yet?",
